  "turns": [
    {
      "turn": 1,
      "doctor_question": "Hello. What brings you in to see me today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S020",
      "patient_response": "Well, honestly, I'm just so overwhelmed right now, and my husband practically begged me to come in. I mean, I work as a mechanic, you know? I’ve been at the same shop for years, and I know cars inside and out. I know every sound an engine makes, every rattle, every hiss. But lately... lately it's not car noises. What brought me in is that I keep hearing this voice. It's a man's voice. And he's not in the shop with me, but I hear him coming right out of the garage vents. At first, I thought maybe it was the guys playing a prank, hooking up a walkie-talkie or something, because it sounds so real. Clear as day, like somebody standing right next to me, breathing on my neck. \n\nAnd it's not just the vents anymore. Sometimes I’ll have my head under the hood of a Chevy or a Ford, just trying to check the alternator or something simple, and the voice comes right out from under the hood. And he says awful things. He tells me... he tells me not to trust my husband. He says my husband is doing things behind my back, plotting things. And then he’ll tell me not to touch certain cars. He’ll say, \"Don't touch that one, it's a trap, they want you to touch it.\" And I just stand there, holding my wrench, terrified to move. I can't get any work done because I'm so scared of what he's going to say next, and I can't even go home and relax because I'm looking at my husband wondering if the voice is right. It's just... it's everywhere, and I can't make it stop.",
