    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "About how long have you been hearing this voice?",
      "targeted_symptom": "psychotic_symptoms_duration",
      "patient_response": "Well, it's... gosh, it's been a while now. I remember it started right around the time the weather started getting cold last year, so... maybe about ten months? Yeah, definitely around ten months. Because I remember I was working on this old Subaru, doing a heater core replacement, which is just a nightmare job anyway because you have to pull the whole dash out, and that's when I first heard it. I thought maybe the wind was just howling through the bay doors, you know how it does in the winter? But then it kept happening, straight through spring and summer, and now we're almost back to winter again. Ten whole months of this guy talking to me. \n\nAnd it's not just the talking, it's... it's the feeling that I'm being watched, or tracked, or something. Like, for those same ten months, ever since the voice started, I've had this awful, creeping feeling that someone is keeping tabs on me. The voice tells me they are. He tells me that my husband is part of it, that they're all watching my every move at the shop, keeping a log of which cars I work on. I even started checking the undercarriage of my own truck for trackers, like those little magnetic GPS things you see in movies? I spend half my lunch break just crawling around on the concrete looking for them, getting grease all over my uniform for nothing, because I never find anything. But the voice says they're there. Ten months of looking over my shoulder, ten months of second-guessing my own husband... it's just exhausting. I can't even remember what it was like to just go to work and turn a wrench without feeling like I'm part of some massive conspiracy.",
