    {
      "turn": 3,
      "doctor_question": "During these past ten months, have you been experiencing persistent feelings of severe depression or sadness?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "No, not really. I mean, I wouldn't say I've been depressed or sad. Not like that. I've just been... terrified, mostly. And exhausted, like I said. But not sad. I mean, I still have energy to do things, you know? I get up, I go to the shop, I crawl under the cars, I look for the trackers. I'm always moving, always doing something. If I were depressed, I wouldn't be able to do all that, right? I'd just be lying in bed all day. But I can't do that. I have to keep moving, I have to keep checking things. \n\nLike last week, I stayed up for almost three days straight just mapping out all the different routes my husband could take to work, trying to see if he was meeting up with anyone to hand over the logs they're keeping on me. I had maps spread out all over the living room floor, drawing lines and calculating distances. You don't do that if you're sad, right? You do that when you're trying to figure things out. And I was feeling pretty good about it, actually, like I was finally getting ahead of them. My mind was just racing, going a million miles a minute, putting all the pieces together. I didn't even feel tired until the fourth day. So no, definitely not sad. Just... busy. And scared. But mostly just trying to stay one step ahead of whatever is going on.",
