      "targeted_symptom": "additional_requirement_2",
      "patient_response": "Well, yeah, actually. It hasn't just been this past week. Honestly, if I look back at the whole ten months since the voice started, most of this past year has been taken over by those high-energy stretches. It's like... it's like a switch flips in my brain, you know? And suddenly I'm just going, going, going. My husband tells me I talk too fast when I get like that, like the words are just spilling out of my mouth before I can even catch them, and I'll start taking on way too much at the shop. I'll tell the service manager I can handle three engine rebuilds at once, which is crazy, right? Nobody can do that. But in my head, I feel like I can. \n\nI feel so driven, like I have this motor inside me that's redlining and I just can't slow down. I'll be bouncing from bay to bay, talking a mile a minute, trying to do a brake job, an alignment, and a transmission flush all at the exact same time. And the whole time, my thoughts are just zooming, connecting dots about the trackers and the logs and my husband. It happens a lot. I'd say the majority of the time since winter, I've been stuck in that overdrive gear. It's just wave after wave of it, where I don't need sleep and I feel like I can figure out the whole conspiracy if I just keep moving fast enough. So, yeah, it's definitely been happening over and over again, almost the whole time the voice has been there.",
