      "turn": 5,
      "doctor_question": "During these ten months, was there ever a period of two weeks or more where your energy and sleep were normal, but you were still hearing the voice?",
      "targeted_symptom": "additional_requirement_3",
      "patient_response": "Yeah, actually... there was a stretch. I think it was right around April, maybe early May? Because the weather was finally breaking and we usually get a huge rush of AC checks, but it was surprisingly dead at the shop for a couple of weeks. And during that time... I don't know, my brain just kind of shifted gears. I wasn't doing the million-miles-a-minute thing anymore. I was actually sleeping. Like, going to bed at 10 PM, waking up at 6 AM, getting a solid eight hours, sometimes even hitting snooze and getting nine, which felt so weird after all those nights staying up for days on end. \n\nI wasn't making these massive plans or trying to take on impossible jobs. I was just... normal? Like, energy-wise, anyway. I was just doing basic tire rotations, oil changes, taking my time, eating my lunch in the breakroom instead of crawling under trucks. But the thing is... the voice didn't stop. Not at all. Even during those quieter few weeks, when my body was actually resting and I wasn't bouncing off the walls, I still heard that guy's voice in the garage every single day. \n\nAnd I still knew—I mean, I fully believed with my whole chest—that my husband and my boss were tracking me. I'd be doing a simple brake pad replacement, totally well-rested, not rushing at all, and the voice would be right there in my ear, echoing off the concrete, telling me that the boss was watching me from the office window. It kept saying he was writing down exactly how long I took on the rotors, logging my movements, and that he was going to hand the whole file over to my husband later that night. So, yeah, my energy definitely slowed down and went back to normal for a good two or three weeks there, but the tracking thing and the voice? They never took a day off. It’s like they don't need to sleep, even when I do, you know? They just keep going.",
